  "remedies": [
    {
      "id": "A125",
      "range": [
        1853,
        1875
      ],
      "contract": "Same five-second deadline and literal context; ForwardDeadline owns the actual Elapsed and exposes it via Error::source."
    },
    {
      "id": "A126",
      "range": [
        1822,
        1851
      ],
      "contract": "All ordinary acquired peers owned immediately; one-shot raw transfer adopted synchronously before future construction; operation and completed/cleanup failure retained with finite finish."
    },
    {
      "id": "A126-queued",
      "range": [
        854,
        1003
      ],
      "contract": "Queued first/sibling requests are retained lexical futures driven under actual first-head readiness and a held challenge, then joined; early exit destroys them. No detached raw queued task remains."
    },
    {
      "id": "A127",
      "range": [
        1947,
        2037
      ],
      "contract": "Actual supervisors own handler JoinSet across accepted task lifetime, signal finite shutdown, drain concrete outcomes, retain accumulated causes across cancelled timed drain and explicit abort/join fallback."
    },
    {
      "id": "A128",
      "range": [
        1019,
        1092
      ],
      "contract": "Record lock poisoning fails before literal 204; clean pre-head EOF classified narrowly; nonempty/truncated heads use original 32KiB bounded read_head and preserve errors."
    },
    {
      "id": "A129",
      "range": [
        2274,
        2357
      ],
      "contract": "Closed/stalled readers propagate unrelated errors; half-close leftover child owned and explicitly joined, including exceptional operation path."
    }
  ],
  "declared_behavior_or_pacing_changes": [
    "Ordinary client setup and requests are scoped to capture their result before explicit peer cleanup. Named client/session handles needed for peer completion are retained; originally temporary inline clients remain temporary.",
    "Queue replaces scheduling yield with an actual first-head signal and an explicit Pending poll of a retained sibling before challenge release. This establishes selected work under a held challenge, not exact pool admission.",
    "All handler errors now matter; JoinSet/watch shutdown replaces detached response workers. Original 300ms next-accept observation remains.",
    "Half-close worker now returns actual leftover bytes, not an unowned raw task; original two-second leftover bound is observed within the worker after replay response and explicit caller client Drop.",
    "The total-deadline fixture now propagates the formerly ignored read_to_end I/O result.",
    "Original ordered assertions use declared joined-value/index aliases and escaped-newline literal indentation equivalence only; raw source hashes are separate."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No Cargo, compilation, Clippy/MSRV or runtime execution of this remedy by author. Integration must run complete forward_proxy callers and all seventeen frozen controls on both native hosts.",
    "Drop aborts outstanding tasks; it is not an explicit synchronous join, and outer five-second timeout/panic/cancellation may prevent observing cleanup outcomes. Explicit normal/error finish is bounded and typed.",
    "Quiet 100/150/300ms observations are finite only; no permanent absence or OS socket leak assertion.",
    "Queue has source-owned lexical cancellation semantics and original route/wire test with strengthened readiness, but no additional independently executed queued-cancellation control in this lane.",
    "Pre-head reset/aborted/broken-pipe are deliberately ordinary disconnects. After any first byte, parser errors propagate. A pending partial head may be cancelled by deliberate shutdown; this does not establish parse success.",
    "Unchanged expected TLS failure bool and byte-at-a-time chunked fixture parsing remain unchanged existing oracles; no claim of full typed trust diagnosis or general HTTP parser correctness.",
    "Shared support and resolved dependency reads are explicitly partial. No whole-codebase, production network, platform or browser parity closure."
  ],
